A SQL body that DECLAREs its own variables is scripted SQL where @name may
be a local, so datasource_undeclared_placeholder bows out entirely
(feature.diagnostics_pipeline A21). Uppercase DECLARE without a leading
colon is SQL, not the SSL :DECLARE keyword, so the document stays SQL.
Statement separators are avoided so datasource_sql_semicolon stays out.
-- input.ds --
DECLARE @nLimit INT
SET @nLimit = 50
SELECT TOP (@nLimit) audit_id, audit_note
FROM audit_entry
WHERE audit_note LIKE @sPattern
-- format --
DECLARE @nLimit INT
SET @nLimit = 50
SELECT TOP (@nLimit) audit_id, audit_note
FROM audit_entry
WHERE audit_note LIKE @sPattern
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
